    "magnetic_field": {
      "file": "rotor_magnetic_field.glb",
      "title": "Rotating field induces current in the bars",
      "description": "The stator's rotating magnetic field sweeps past the rotor bars faster than they move (slip ≈ 0.5–5 % at load). This induces voltage and large currents in the short-circuited cage; the current in the field produces torque. Bars are skewed (≈ one slot pitch) to smooth torque and reduce noise. Broken bars or cracked end rings show up as current side-bands at slip frequency and as hot spots.",
